# A dependency finding has to say which advisory it matched. Without the id there
# is nothing to look up and nothing to act on, and a reader is left to guess why
# the version in front of them is being reported at all.

test "sca: a dependency finding names the advisory it matched"
  lang python
  expect VYQL-SCA-001
  expect_evidence VYQL-SCA-001 CVE-2018-1000656
  file app.py
  code
  ```
  import flask
  ```
  file requirements.txt
  code
  ```
  flask==0.12.2
  ```

# An entry with an upper bound asks a different question from one with a lower
# bound: not "which version is installed" but "what does the declaration permit".
# Reported without that sentence, a current release looks flagged for being
# current, which reads as the comparison running backwards.

test "sca: an upper-bound advisory says the declared range is what matched"
  lang python
  expect VYQL-SCA-001
  expect_evidence VYQL-SCA-001 permits versions above 2.31.0
  file app.py
  code
  ```
  import requests
  ```
  file requirements.txt
  code
  ```
  requests==2.34.2
  ```
